 non-null even for slices of length zero. Thus, the use of a null pointer leads to undefined behavior.","date":"2026-05-12","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["git2"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/git2-rs/pull/1250","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[">=0.21.0"],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"git2","version":"0.20.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"7b88256088d75a56f8ecfa070513a775dd9107f6530ef14919dac831af9cfe2b","dependencies":[{"name":"bitflags","version":"2.13.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.189","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libgit2-sys","version":"0.18.8+1.9.7","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"log","version":"0.4.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"url","version":"2.5.8","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0184","package":"git2","title":"Potential undefined behavior with Signature from a buffer-created BlameHunk","description":"When a `Blame` is created via `Blame::blame_buffer()`, and a `BlameHunk` is retrieved, the pointers to the original author, original committer, final author, and final committer may be null if unavailable. The corresponding `BlameHunk` methods then create `Signature`s based on null pointers; attempting to access the data of the `Signature`s leads to dereferencing null pointers.","date":"2026-05-13","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["git2"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/git2-rs/pull/1254","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[">=0.21.0"],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"glib","version":"0.18.5","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"233daaf6e83ae6a12a52055f568f9d7cf4671dabb78ff9560ab6da230ce00ee5","dependencies":[{"name":"bitflags","version":"2.13.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-channel","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-core","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-executor","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-task","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"futures-util","version":"0.3.34","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"gio-sys","version":"0.18.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"glib-macros","version":"0.18.5","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"glib-sys","version":"0.18.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"gobject-sys","version":"0.18.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.189","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"memchr","version":"2.8.3","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"once_cell","version":"1.21.4","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"smallvec","version":"1.15.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"thiserror","version":"1.0.69","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2024-0429","package":"glib","title":"Unsoundness in `Iterator` and `DoubleEndedIterator` impls for `glib::VariantStrIter`","description":"The `VariantStrIter::impl_get` function (called internally by implementations of the `Iterator` and `DoubleEndedIterator` traits for this type) was unsound, resulting in undefined behaviour.\n\nAn immutable reference `&p` to a `*mut libc::c_char` pointer initialized to `NULL` was passed as an argument to a C function that that mutates the pointer behind `&p` in-place (i.e. as an out-argument), which was unsound. After changes in recent versions of the Rust compiler, these unsound writes through `&p` now seem to be completely disregarded when building the `glib` crate with optimizations.\n\nThis subsequently caused all calls of `VariantStrIter::impl_get` to violate the safety requirements of the `std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr` function - which requires its argument to be a valid pointer to a C-style string - resulting in crashes due to `NULL` pointer dereferences.\n\nThis was fixed by passing the out-argument pointer explitly as `&mut p` instead of `&p`.\n\nThis issue has been present since this code was initially added in `glib` v0.15.0. The mismatch in mutability was likely missed (and not raised as an error by the compiler) because the C function wrapped by `VariantStrIter::impl_get` is variadic (`glib_sys::g_variant_get_child`), and the pointer in question is one of the variadic arguments.","date":"2024-03-30","aliases":["GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk-rs-core/pull/1343","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":{"arch":[],"os":[],"functions":{"glib::VariantStrIter::last":[">=0.15.0, <0.20.0"],"glib::VariantStrIter::next":[">=0.15.0, <0.20.0"],"glib::VariantStrIter::next_back":[">=0.15.0, <0.20.0"],"glib::VariantStrIter::nth":[">=0.15.0, <0.20.0"],"glib::VariantStrIter::nth_back":[">=0.15.0, <0.20.0"]}},"versions":{"patched":[">=0.20.0"],"unaffected":["<0.15.0"]}}]}}

